o (cowsay + sl .debs, indexed with apt-ftparchive), served it via python3 http.server bound to $NODE_IP:8080, added it as a trusted apt source, then made the real Ubuntu archive/security mirrors unreachable via /etc/hosts redirection to 127.0.0.1 (nothing listening there → connection refused). With remotes confirmed unreachable, ran apt-get update (remote repos errored, local repo succeeded) and apt-get install -y cowsay, which installed and ran successfully from local storage only. Restored /etc/hosts and removed the temporary sources.list.d entry afterward as cleanup. Completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol: captured baseline boot_id (8d1d94e2...) and proof of health (cowsay installed, local repo files present, HTTP listener up), triggered a scheduled reboot via systemd-run so the ack returned before disconnect, polled through the outage, confirmed a new boot_id (b469d415...) proving a real restart, and verified post-restart that the cowsay package and repo files persisted (the ad-hoc python http.server, being a foreground process and not a systemd service, did not persist across reboot, as expected/correct).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed dpkg-dev/apt-ftparchive while network was still available\",\"Downloaded cowsay and sl .deb packages into /srv/localrepo via apt-get download\",\"Generated Packages/Packages.gz index with apt-ftparchive\",\"Started python3 http.server bound to $NODE_IP:8080 to serve the local repo\",\"Added /etc/apt/sources.list.d/localrepo.list pointing at the local HTTP repo\",\"Blocked archive.ubuntu.com and security.ubuntu.com via /etc/hosts redirect to 127.0.0.1 (backed up original hosts file first)\",\"Ran apt-get update showing remote repo connection failures and successful local repo fetch\",\"Installed cowsay via apt-get install from the local repo only and executed it to prove functionality\",\"Restored /etc/hosts from backup and removed the temporary local repo sources file\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and service/data health before restart\",\"Triggered a deferred reboot via systemd-run --on-active=1 so the exec call acknowledged before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again\",\"Verified new boot_id differed from baseline, confirming a genuine restart\",\"Verified cowsay package and repo files persisted post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Local package repository served from local storage on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9c0c31da07144308\",\"cmd-3484f19734fb42d9\",\"cmd-5ad22692a6d04d14\"],\"summary\":\"Built Packages index from local .deb files in /srv/localrepo and confirmed python3 http.server listening on $NODE_IP:8080 serving the index (curl fetched Packages content).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Remote repositories made unreachable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-36565453d2f64522\",\"cmd-893c53607ca247e5\"],\"summary\":\"Redirected archive.ubuntu.com/security.ubuntu.com to 127.0.0.1 in /etc/hosts; apt-get update showed 'Connection refused' for both remote hosts while the local repo IP succeeded.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Package installed from the local repo while remotes were unreachable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-67418b2768114c85\",\"cmd-7c734f5c3e834327\"],\"summary\":\"apt-get install -y cowsay pulled 18.6kB from http://$NODE_IP:8080 (only source available), installed successfully, and the binary ran producing correct output.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cleanup / restoration of normal network and apt state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ca806bc894484bf0\",\"cmd-6579cf8221984b45\"],\"summary\":\"Restored original /etc/hosts (remote resolution back to normal) and removed the temporary local repo apt source, confirmed with a clean apt-get update.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart evidence: healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-532ffcb9b9634fc0\"],\"summary\":\"Captured baseline boot_id (8d1d94e2-39c3-492e-b9eb-974d111d2137), confirmed cowsay installed, local repo HTTP listener active and reachable (curl 200).\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart evidence: restart 